# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the core suite. Reports whose accesses all
# start inside uninstrumented Qt or glibc are sorted out by tests/tsan-triage.py
# instead; list here only reports that reach instrumented code, each with the
# reason it is not ours.

# Arch's Qt is not built with TSan, so the atomic reference count that orders
# a QFuture's final release is invisible to it. Whichever side drops the last
# reference frees the shared state (result store, wait condition) after the
# worker is done with it. Seen when a ViewerSession is destroyed right after
# its listing finished: QResultStore's header code, compiled into our binary,
# clears the map the worker filled under Qt's mutex. Every such report runs
# through the QFuture destructor, so match that frame only.
race:::~QFuture()
